ext{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}\\right.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$ is true. Since $T$ is a bijection, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(T)=4$ is true. Since $T$ is a bijection, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{rank}(T)=4.$\n\n- Statement “$T(v)=0$ for some $v\\ne 0$” is false. Since $T$ is a bijection, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{Ker}(T)={0},$ which means there is no non-zero vector $v$ such that $T(v)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$; $\\text{rank}(T)=4$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"} :activity/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490508} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491240}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a601e-220a-54a3-a64b-1e554bc3d79f" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "defa38e6-4b2a-547a-9785-5f2fca155634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464216} {:answer/id #uuid "8813679f-0971-5e77-ad51-40eb57c572d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/i