er-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465044}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c4507db3-2027-5030-88fd-955381171b17" :question/math-academy-id "q-141569" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{4}\\to {R}^{4}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If $\\text{nullity}(T)=4,$ then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{4}$ into ${R}^{4},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\left\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=4 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}\\right.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{4}$ is false. Since $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0,$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement “$T$ is not invertible” is true. Indeed, since $\\text{nullity}(T)\\ne 0,$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that $T$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 4$ is true. Indeed, since $T$ is not invertible, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$T$ is not invertible”; $\\text{rank}(T)\\ne 4$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "113a601e-220a-54a3-a64b-1e554bc3d79f" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d41688-d441-5144-8654-a972f8be5b21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464222} {:answer/id #uuid "8e89bfdc-e0ea-5cb6-9225-4a56ce59f56c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e89bfdc-e0ea-5cb6-9225-4a56ce59f56c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464223} :answer-field/id #uuid "72f72fce-9abb-5a6c-9689-b54025b14cfe" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7398f9ee-d9ed-555a-acc0-735e4fdaa78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464224} {:answer/id #uuid "73635a76-1329-52e8-bd4c-7b079d5a02a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7398f9ee-d9ed-555a-acc0-735e4fdaa78b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464224} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5214e79-29e2-5009-b0e1-02450bcb5417" :answer-field/key "$\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{6}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465046} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a9be739-fcf6-5a16-8afe-a003efb9a3a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464226} {:answer/id #uuid "786a548c-28ba-5e22-835f-02191b3b2922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "786a548c-28ba-5e22-835f-02191b3b2922" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464227} :answer-field/id #uuid "53569532-51d7-56fd-b1b2-b9c1761560c6" :answer-field/key "$T$ is not a bijection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2805dfb0-8d9a-5775-8051-a005b74b03a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-141584" :question/problem "Let $T:{R}^{6}\\to {R}^{6}$ be a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n*If ${v}_{1}\\ne {v}_{2}$ vectors such that $T({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})$, then $\\underline{\\phantom{xxxxxx}}.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{6}$ into ${R}^{6},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\left\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=6 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nSince $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that\n\n$$\nT({v}_{1})=T({v}_{2})\\,⟹\\,T({v}_{1}-{v}_{2})=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$ is true. Since ${v}_{1}-{v}_{2}\\in \\text{Ker}(T)$ and ${v}_{1}\\ne {v}_{2},$ we must have that $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{6}$ is false. According to the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0},$ the transformation $T$ and the matrix $T$ are not invertible. Since $T$ is not invertible, by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have that $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{6}.$\n\n- Statement “$T$ is not a bijection” is true. Since $\\text{Im}(T)\\ne {R}^{6},$ the invertible matrix theorem implies that the transformation $T$ is not a bijection.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Ker}(T)\\ne {0}$; “$T$ is not a bijection” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"} :activity/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490508} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491273}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124521 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9d77214-796e-558f-a364-00ae3e25cc13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a41ae6c-0d04-54af-b7e1-66f17408a105" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450600} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e20032-0a94-5027-bacb-72669ad1d4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7e20032-0a94-5027-bacb-72669ad1d4f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450601} :answer-field/id #uuid "