44ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-38905" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true given that $T:{R}^{6}\\to {R}^{6}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T,$ and $T$ is a bijection?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $T$ is a linear transformation from ${R}^{6}$ into ${R}^{6},$ the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n $T$ is a bijection (an invertible transformation) $\\,⟺\\,\\left\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=6 \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)={0} \\\\  & \\text{nullity}(T)=0\\end{aligned}\\right.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$ is true. Since $T$ is a bijection, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{6}$ is true. Since $T$ is a bijection, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{6}.$\n\n- Statement $\\text{rank}(T)=6$ is true. Since $T$ is a bijection, the invertible matrix theorem implies that $\\text{rank}(T)=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{Ker}(T)={0}$; $\\text{Im}(T)={R}^{6}$; $\\text{rank}(T)=6$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326728 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124521 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9d77214-796e-558f-a364-00ae3e25cc13" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049371 :topic/id #uuid "ef6bb570-cff7-5ef3-a4ba-79063f5d81ad" :topic/math-academy-id 1962 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Linear Transformations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3b6b69e-fdda-5b48-8cbe-b6154cd7c5d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450606} {:answer/id #uuid "97c3efcd-f3c2-540f-afcf-4d2de2e5f841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499